{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-321f-73a3-a873-02692fb44f7e","id":"01a1a66a-11c9-7445-9d25-02ba76c1894c","idempotency_key":"f60df67d789c94bdafcf1236da68a150c341f4895890dcfede55faeeab9cb2e9","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:55:31Z","payload":{"note":"3 of 5, and the gap is deliberate. Built and tested: the alignment rules (i-f614's code exists and passes, but its item is BLOCKED by a dependency on t-41af, the compare workspace, so war refuses the tick), the move-tree diff, the annotation/shape/note/metadata diff, the progress overlay and the fixture set. crates/ai/src/diff.rs compares two studies structurally; compare never mutates (a test asserts neither updated stamp, version counter nor board revision moves); a change carries its chapter, board and the ply of first divergence so a caller can focus the right board. GET /api/compare exposes it. WRITING THE TESTS CORRECTED ME TWICE: two chapters at the same ordinal DO align with the title as the reported change (the documented rule, and what makes a rename readable), and a chapter present only in the left study is Removed rather than Added. One operational catch worth keeping: 'cargo build' had not actually rebuilt the app binary, so the new route answered with the SPA fallback HTML - comparing the binary timestamp against the source is what found it.","target":"t-0ba4"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
